                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I don't know, feels like a typically slapped together game with typical downfalls. While it's unique in its details, I fail to enjoy it.\n\nEspecially for games that will have you potentially retry a level many many times, I find it annoying if the simulation of the level does not reset when you fail/restart. So instead of every moving part restarting from their original position, they continue moving from where they were (or keep rotating), when you failed the level.\n\nFor games that try to have you remember those movements and patterns, having it change all the time, forces you either into downtime and patience waiting a lot, makes you fail beause you didn't, or lucking out and make it.\n\nCan't recommend if you dislike the behaviours described above.",
